## Compound Component Pattern

Use the compound pattern (subcomponent files + context) when:

- The component has 3 or more meaningfully separate slots (e.g. `AppModal`: header, body, footer)
- Sub-parts need independent props
- Sub-parts may be omitted, reordered, or reused elsewhere

Follow AGENTS.md and the `11-add-compound-component.mdc` rule. Example:

```tsx
<AppModal>
  <AppModal.Header title="Confirm booking" onClose={close} />
  <AppModal.Body>...</AppModal.Body>
  <AppModal.Footer>
    <AppButton variant="primary" onClick={confirm}>Confirm</AppButton>
  </AppModal.Footer>
</AppModal>
```

File structure for compound components:

```
AppModal/
├── index.tsx                 ← root, owns state, renders Context.Provider, attaches subcomponents
├── AppModal.Header.tsx
├── AppModal.Body.tsx
├── AppModal.Footer.tsx
├── AppModal.context.ts       ← Context + useAppModalContext()
├── AppModal.types.ts
├── AppModal.module.scss      ← root + shared styles
├── AppModal.Header.module.scss
├── AppModal.Body.module.scss
├── AppModal.Footer.module.scss
├── AppModal.stories.tsx
└── assets/                   ← only if colocated SVGs are needed
```

